      "text": "/skill:tidy-recipe-authoring\n\nCreate tidy recipes for workbook `48cc7c74817cf57e5de9d01f94b1daa5b4d88f30ddc3f057bd20a21ebecce9eb--recorded-crime-offenders-2017-18-cube-4-source.xlsx`.\n\n- Publication: Recorded Crime — Offenders (Australian Bureau of Statistics)\n- Release or year: 2017-18\n- Sheets needing a recipe: 5 of 5\n\n| sheet | sheet_sha256 | current recipe |\n|---|---|---|\n| \"Contents\" | a7289446f8e3f41caf91dde92ffb3b93fe98eb421f298dfdb141b5cc2c7f9d22 | missing |\n| \"Table 22\" | fa4c0498c0280aee724bb93b27fecc7d177b0e29db7f5ada3146162671f2b97f | missing |\n| \"Table 23\" | 92621eab2a469facb9990064790a48bb9f3772256dc3ff361858d9efa2499cf4 | missing |\n| \"Table 24\" | dc630384b761670b032a1f75f620c73ecd0f23412e1a271006325606814651a0 | missing |\n| \"Table 25\" | 7c45ce96565600dd3d08e8187907290c37807bc771f894837026d01476696de4 | missing |\n\nRelated workbooks:\n- None\n\nWork through every sheet listed above using the skill's workflow. Use\n`codemode` scripts to call the recipe tools, and batch the work: for example,\nlist the workbook and check templates for all sheets in one script, then read\ngrids and test recipes a few sheets at a time. Keep script output short.\n\nName dimensions from `dictionary/dimensions.csv` (see the skill's\n`references/naming.md`); declare any name it lacks in `new_dimensions`.\n\nWrite each recipe to `tidy-recipes/<sheet_sha256>.json` and finish every sheet\nwith `submit_recipe`. You may only write recipe files for this workbook.\n\nEnd with one line per sheet: `sheet | kind | status | records | remaining failures`."
